name 'ai-generated-design-postassessment-q6_2025'

question 'A community news site notices that people using screen readers have trouble navigating its pages because the articles don\'t have proper heading tags. Which accessibility principle is being overlooked?'

wrong 'Operable – users can\'t easily move through the content'
wrong 'Understandable – users can\'t follow the site\'s main idea'
wrong 'Perceivable – users can\'t see the colors or images'
right 'Robust – the site doesn\'t work well with assistive technologies'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lessons 6, 11
MARKDOWN
